<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Launcher foreground: the 512x512 round badge, inset so its outer rings
    survive the launcher mask. Background is transparent (as in EdgeCase and
    ShadeCase), so the badge's own edge is the icon's edge on every mask shape.

      badge diameter               460 of 512 px  = 89.8% of the layer
      visible adaptive-icon area   72 of 108 dp   = 66.7% of the layer

    At inset 0 the badge would be 97 dp across and the circular mask would cut
    off its outer rings. A 13% inset per side scales the layer to 74%, putting
    the badge at 71.8 dp: its rim sits just inside the 72 dp mask circle.
    If the artwork is ever re-cut with a different margin, recompute this.

    The PNG is in drawable-nodpi so it is decoded at its real 512 px instead
    of being upscaled by screen density. No per-density mipmap PNGs exist:
    minSdk 30 always uses this adaptive icon.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/icon_round"
    android:inset="13%" />
